      <activity id="0a0eed34-4b6d-552c-984d-bbe1176dbb93" activityNameId="aa1ae78e-ad69-5d84-babd-38abcacf21e3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Magnesium-alloy, AZ91, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Magnesium-alloy, AZ91, at plant
The magnesium alloy AZ91D is the most common one for the production of die-castings. It contains 9.1% aluminium and small amounts of zinc and manganese. Environmental impacts of production are only known from a summarized inventory. It is assumed that magnesium for this alloy has been produced in a new production plant.;
Synonyms: M11916, DIN GD-MgAl9Zn1; 
UUID: cb518d31-41bf-3501-b2db-2e8b0ad9e1d8
Production of alloy from primary metals, no extra infrastructure.
Location: Data for 1 producer
Technology: Production of magnesium alloy from primary metals, no recycling of input materials.
Time period: Environmental report
Production volume: na
Sampling: Environmental data from an important producer 
Extrapolations: From 1 producer to average Europe
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cb518d31-41bf-3501-b2db-2e8b0ad9e1d8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
